00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:05,171
Beyond First Impressions I had dismissed my new neighbour as snobbish because

2
00:00:05,184 --> 00:00:10,605
he rarely spoke He was bald wore formal clothes and looked decidedly

3
00:00:10,618 --> 00:00:15,829
uneasy at our first gathering I foolishly treated those details as evidence

4
00:00:15,842 --> 00:00:21,816
of his personality That judgment now seems shameful When a storm damaged

5
00:00:21,829 --> 00:00:26,105
the street he worked tirelessly to help He did not preach about

6
00:00:26,118 --> 00:00:30,803
generosity or deliver a sermon on duty He simply offered time and

7
00:00:30,816 --> 00:00:35,092
tools I felt shame at my earlier assumption and tried to make

8
00:00:35,105 --> 00:00:39,632
amends The experience taught me not to resent someone for failing to

9
00:00:39,645 --> 00:00:45,276
fit my expectations A tolerant community must make room for different manners

10
00:00:45,368 --> 00:00:50,421
including silence A person may be reserved without being rude just as

11
00:00:50,434 --> 00:00:55,000
a lively manner need not indicate goodness We ought to replace petty

12
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:59,947
labels with patient attention The requisite first step is often to admit

13
00:00:59,961 --> 00:01:01,566
